<title>ITALY: Milan airports air cargo traffic down 5.8pc in Jan. [CORRECTED 14:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Milan airports air cargo traffic down 5.8pc in Jan. [CORRECTED 14:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by Milan's airport system slipped to 12,531 tonnes in January, down 5.8 percent on the same period 1996, operating company SEA said.</p>
<p>				Total Milan system</p>
<p>				Jan 97	  Jan 96</p>
<p> Total Cargo (tonnes)    12,531	  13,298</p>
<p> Mail (tonnes)		1,059	     949 (Corrects figures for Mail)</p>
<p> Passengers		 872,000	 786,000</p>
<p> Aircraft movements	15,683	  14,264</p>
<p>		     Linate Airport	 Malpensa Airport</p>
<p>		     Jan 97    Jan 96     Jan 97	Jan 96</p>
<p> Total Cargo	4,877     4,861	7,654	 8,437</p>
<p> Mail		 1,030	 925	   29	    24</p>
<p> (Corrects Malpensa Mail figures to tonnes from kilos)</p>
<p> Passengers     872,000   785,957    302,967     279,408</p>
<p> Aircraft	  12,565    11,552	3,118	 2,658</p>
<p>movements</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
